WEBVTT

00:00:14.605 --> 00:00:16.605
-McQueen, let go!
-Never!

00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:21.125
-They're coming your way.
-Let's go!

00:00:29.325 --> 00:00:30.685
Give it up, McMissile.

00:00:40.165 --> 00:00:41.685
(RAPID BLEEPING)

00:00:47.005 --> 00:00:50.485
-HOLLEY: Mater, stop!
-No way! You could get hurt.

00:00:56.405 --> 00:00:57.805
Oh, no.

00:01:11.645 --> 00:01:13.445
(SNARLING)

00:01:14.365 --> 00:01:16.365
(GROANING)

00:01:19.005 --> 00:01:21.845
Mater, we've got to get
that bomb off you.

00:01:21.885 --> 00:01:22.925
Bomb?

00:01:23.005 --> 00:01:25.005
Yeah, they strapped it to me
to kill you as a back-up plan.

00:01:25.045 --> 00:01:28.085
Back-up plan?
Mater, who put a bomb on you?

00:01:28.885 --> 00:01:31.365
You! Why didn't my death ray kill you?

00:01:31.445 --> 00:01:32.805
Death ray?

00:01:32.885 --> 00:01:34.205
Turn off the bomb, Zündapp!

00:01:34.245 --> 00:01:36.805
Are you all so dense?
It's voice-activated.

00:01:36.885 --> 00:01:39.005
Everything is voice-activated
these days.

00:01:39.045 --> 00:01:41.405
Deactivate! Deactivate!

00:01:41.485 --> 00:01:43.165
AUTOMATED VOICE:
Voice denied.

00:01:44.885 --> 00:01:46.445
-Huh!
-Oops.

00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:49.045
Did I forget to mention
that it can only be disarmed

00:01:49.085 --> 00:01:50.845
by the one who activated it?

00:01:51.125 --> 00:01:53.045
-Say it.
-Deactivate.

00:01:54.045 --> 00:01:55.525
AUTOMATED VOICE:
Voice denied.

00:01:58.445 --> 00:02:02.045
I'm not the one who activated it.
Would anyone else like to try?

00:02:02.885 --> 00:02:05.245
-You read my mind.
-He was getting on my nerves.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.925
-What do we do?
-It's very simple. You blow up.

00:02:09.285 --> 00:02:13.085
I'm going out on a limb here. These are
the guys that want me dead, correct?

00:02:13.125 --> 00:02:15.605
-It's nothing personal.
-Fellers, listen.

00:02:15.725 --> 00:02:19.725
I know what you're going through.
Everybody's been laughing at me too.

00:02:20.925 --> 00:02:24.085
But becoming powerful and rich
beyond your wildest dreams

00:02:24.125 --> 00:02:26.605
ain't gonna make you feel better.

00:02:27.405 --> 00:02:29.445
Yeah, but it's worth a shot.

00:02:38.765 --> 00:02:39.925
Pit stop.

00:02:44.165 --> 00:02:46.165
Not today, boys.

00:02:49.965 --> 00:02:51.485
(YELLS)

00:02:55.805 --> 00:02:56.805
Retreat!

00:02:59.725 --> 00:03:01.445
Thanks for the help, Corporal.

00:03:01.485 --> 00:03:03.885
Anything for one of Pop's mates.

00:03:07.965 --> 00:03:09.925
(SPEAKS ITALIAN)

00:03:09.965 --> 00:03:11.965
What's he saying? What's wrong?

00:03:12.045 --> 00:03:14.045
None of his wrenches fit the bolts.

00:03:16.365 --> 00:03:18.325
I get it. I get it!

00:03:18.405 --> 00:03:20.725
-I know what needs to be done.
-Then do it!

00:03:20.805 --> 00:03:22.965
What? No. I can't do it.

00:03:23.085 --> 00:03:25.005
Nobody takes me seriously.

00:03:25.125 --> 00:03:28.205
I know that now.
This ain't Radiator Springs.

00:03:28.325 --> 00:03:30.005
Yes, it is.

00:03:30.285 --> 00:03:32.925
Look, you're yourself
in Radiator Springs.

00:03:33.005 --> 00:03:34.965
Be yourself here.

00:03:35.005 --> 00:03:37.005
And if people aren't taking you
seriously,

00:03:37.085 --> 00:03:39.725
then they need to change, not you.

00:03:39.805 --> 00:03:41.925
I know that
because I was wrong before.

00:03:42.525 --> 00:03:44.605
Now, you can do this. You're the bomb.

00:03:44.725 --> 00:03:46.325
Thanks, buddy.

00:03:46.405 --> 00:03:48.925
No, you're the actual bomb.
Now, let's go!

00:03:49.005 --> 00:03:51.005
Oh, right. Hang on!

00:03:52.685 --> 00:03:54.685
Where's he going?

00:03:56.365 --> 00:03:58.325
-Computer!
-COMPUTER: Yes, Agent Mater?

00:03:58.365 --> 00:04:01.245
I need that thing you done before
to get me away from McQueen!

00:04:01.365 --> 00:04:02.565
Request acknowledged.

00:04:06.125 --> 00:04:08.325
-Mater?
-Now I need you to do the chute!

00:04:08.365 --> 00:04:10.365
The second kind, not the first!

00:04:10.405 --> 00:04:12.245
COMPUTER: Deploying chute.

00:04:36.005 --> 00:04:37.605
Who's winning the race?

00:04:41.925 --> 00:04:44.405
-Back off! Back away!
-It's Lightning McQueen!

00:04:44.485 --> 00:04:46.645
No, it's OK! Tell 'em, Mater. Explain.

00:04:46.765 --> 00:04:48.285
Okay.

00:04:48.405 --> 00:04:49.885
Somebody's been sabotaging

00:04:49.965 --> 00:04:52.245
the racers and hurtin' the cars,
and I know who.

00:04:52.365 --> 00:04:54.085
Oh, wait. Your Majesty.

00:04:54.205 --> 00:04:56.205
Bomb! It's a bomb!

00:04:56.925 --> 00:04:59.405
-Everybody, down!
-Back up! Move it!

00:04:59.485 --> 00:05:00.525
(ALL CLAMORING)

00:05:01.565 --> 00:05:03.565
Get off the stage! Move it!

00:05:03.645 --> 00:05:06.645
Hold your fire! He can't disarm it!

00:05:06.765 --> 00:05:10.085
Mater, I don't know what you're doing,
but stand down now.

00:05:10.205 --> 00:05:12.965
This ain't nothing at all
like Radiator Springs.

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:15.005
Mater, just cut to the chase.

00:05:15.085 --> 00:05:17.045
Okay. It's him.

00:05:17.085 --> 00:05:20.165
What? Me? You've got to be crazy.

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:22.205
I figured it out when I realized

00:05:22.285 --> 00:05:25.765
y'all attached this ticking time bomb
with Whitworth bolts -

00:05:25.845 --> 00:05:29.285
the same bolts that hold together that
old British engine from the photograph.

00:05:30.565 --> 00:05:31.845
-Holley! Show that picture.
-OK.

00:05:32.285 --> 00:05:34.925
I remembered what they say
about old British engines:

00:05:35.045 --> 00:05:37.645
if there ain't no oil under 'em,
there ain't no oil in 'em.

00:05:37.805 --> 00:05:39.685
What is he talking about?

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:42.405
It was you leaking oil
at the party in Japan.

00:05:42.445 --> 00:05:44.125
You just blamed it on me.

00:05:44.245 --> 00:05:46.805
Electric cars don't use oil, you twit.

00:05:46.885 --> 00:05:50.125
Then you're fakin' it.
You didn't convert to no electric.

00:05:51.285 --> 00:05:54.125
If we pop that hood,
we'll see that engine from that picture.

00:05:54.525 --> 00:05:57.565
This lorry's crazy!
He's going to kill us all!

00:05:58.725 --> 00:05:59.885
Stay away!

00:05:59.965 --> 00:06:03.845
But Sir Axlerod created the race.
Why would he want to hurt anyone?

00:06:03.925 --> 00:06:07.485
To make allinol look bad so
everybody'd go back to using oil.

00:06:07.525 --> 00:06:10.125
He said it himself
with that disguised voice.

00:06:10.165 --> 00:06:14.245
Disguised voice? What are you
talking about? You're nuts, you are!

00:06:14.325 --> 00:06:17.165
This is going nowhere fast.
We really should go, Grandmother.

00:06:17.405 --> 00:06:19.805
One moment, I'd like to see
where this is going.

00:06:20.885 --> 00:06:22.685
Mater, he created allinol.

00:06:22.845 --> 00:06:24.525
But what if he found that huge oil field

00:06:24.685 --> 00:06:27.165
just as the world was trying to find
something else?

00:06:27.245 --> 00:06:31.085
What if he came up with allinol
just to make alternative fuel look bad?

00:06:31.165 --> 00:06:34.005
"What if?"
You're basing this on a "what if"?

00:06:34.085 --> 00:06:36.165
-Okay, that's it.
-Lads, clear out.

00:06:36.285 --> 00:06:39.405
Wait! Somebody save me!
The lorry's crazy!

00:06:39.525 --> 00:06:41.325
-Keep away, you idiot!
-Mater!

00:06:42.165 --> 00:06:44.685
-Mater!
-Someone do something!

00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:49.805
You're insane, you are! Deactivate!

00:06:51.485 --> 00:06:55.525
COMPUTER: Bomb deactivated.
Have a nice day, Sir Axlerod.

